    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "After prior long-acting cabotegravir PrEP: do integrase resistance testing first when feasible. If ART must start b4 results: a boosted PI (darunavir/cobicistat or darunavir/ritonavir + emtricitabine or lamivudine) may be used as a temp empiric option."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Darunavir 800 mg + ritonavir 100 mg QD w food (⍉darunavir resistance); 600 mg + ritonavir 100 mg BID w food if ± one darunavir resistance substitution."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Always take darunavir w ritonavir and food; otherwise it can lose efficacy."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "↓dose ritonavir (eg, 100 mg daily) boosts other PIs by inhibiting their hepatic met. PIs (CYP450) raise levels of other drugs; darunavir/ritonavir = CI w narrow-therapeutic-index drugs highly dep on CYP3A. St John's wort lowers PI and NNRTI levels."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Drug-induced hepatitis can occur:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " check liver funct b4 and during therapy, esp w chronic hepatitis, cirrhosis or raised baseline transaminases."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
